Silo patch 0014 — ntdll: keep more LFH block groups alive

Origin: Zagrios/voile-wine, commit 4b5fbc36 (2026-09-26, author Zagrios), a backport of Proton's Wine 31d70e4e5db2
(ValveSoftware/wine). License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like Wine. Hunks unchanged.

Why Silo carries it: a small Proton fix taken on its merit (user, 2026-11-14). Each LFH bin keeps as many free block
groups as it ever had in use (instead of one per affinity slot), so a heap that frees and reallocates many blocks
reuses its groups instead of mapping new ones. dlls/ntdll/heap.c, +8/-2. No regression in the 2026-11-14 checks.
Not taken from the same batch: voile-wine 460580a5 (event in-process sync sent with create_event) — it changes the
server protocol and msync timing, and gave no measurable gain on TEKKEN 8; kept in .wine-build/experiments only.

---- original commit below (git format-patch, unchanged) ----

From 4b5fbc3639f546e154ba762de42b6eb1d049b7cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zagrios <40181755+Zagrios@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:50:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Keep more LFH block groups alive.

Let each LFH bin keep as many free block groups as it ever had in use,
instead of one per affinity slot, so a heap that frees and reallocates
many blocks reuses its groups rather than mapping new ones. From
Proton's Wine: 31d70e4e5db2 (ValveSoftware/wine).
---
 dlls/ntdll/heap.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/heap.c b/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
index 78fa83d0..66607c85 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
@@ -267,6 +267,9 @@ struct bin
 
     /* list of groups with free blocks */
     SLIST_HEADER groups;
+    LONG group_alloc;
+    LONG group_freed;
+    LONG group_max;
 
     /* array of affinity reserved groups, interleaved with other bins to keep
      * all pointers of the same affinity and different bin grouped together,
@@ -1864,7 +1867,7 @@ static inline ULONG heap_current_thread_affinity(void)
 /* acquire a group from the bin, thread takes ownership of a shared group or allocates a new one */
 static struct group *heap_acquire_bin_group( struct heap *heap, ULONG flags, SIZE_T block_size, struct bin *bin )
 {
-    ULONG affinity = NtCurrentTeb()->HeapVirtualAffinity;
+    ULONG affinity = NtCurrentTeb()->HeapVirtualAffinity, count;
     struct group *group;
     SLIST_ENTRY *entry;
 
@@ -1874,6 +1877,8 @@ static struct group *heap_acquire_bin_group( struct heap *heap, ULONG flags, SIZ
     if ((entry = RtlInterlockedPopEntrySList( &bin->groups )))
         return CONTAINING_RECORD( entry, struct group, entry );
 
+    count = InterlockedIncrement( &bin->group_alloc ) - ReadNoFence( &bin->group_freed );
+    if (count > ReadAcquire( &bin->group_max )) WriteRelease( &bin->group_max, count );
     return group_allocate( heap, flags, block_size );
 }
 
@@ -1889,12 +1894,13 @@ static NTSTATUS heap_release_bin_group( struct heap *heap, ULONG flags, struct b
         return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 
     /* try re-using the block group instead of releasing it */
-    if (RtlQueryDepthSList( &bin->groups ) <= ARRAY_SIZE(affinity_mapping))
+    if (RtlQueryDepthSList( &bin->groups ) <= ReadAcquire( &bin->group_max ))
     {
         RtlInterlockedPushEntrySList( &bin->groups, &group->entry );
         return STATUS_SUCCESS;
     }
 
+    InterlockedIncrement( &bin->group_freed );
     return group_release( heap, flags, bin, group );
 }
 
